Kernova's fixes to Periphery, which Tools/install-periphery.sh applies to the
pinned tag before it builds it.

AppIntentsRetainer: the App Intents metadata the build extracts lists every
type that conforms to an App Intents protocol, including one that conforms
through a protocol of its own refining it (`ConsentingIntent: AppIntent`).
Periphery 3.8.0 retains only a type whose inheritance clause names the App
Intents protocol itself, so this walks inherited protocols as
SourceGraph.isCodable does for Codable.

diff --git a/Sources/SourceGraph/Mutators/AppIntentsRetainer.swift b/Sources/SourceGraph/Mutators/AppIntentsRetainer.swift
index ae2b655..9253528 100644
--- a/Sources/SourceGraph/Mutators/AppIntentsRetainer.swift
+++ b/Sources/SourceGraph/Mutators/AppIntentsRetainer.swift
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ import Configuration
 import Foundation
 import Shared
 
-/// Retains types conforming to App Intents protocols.
+/// Retains types conforming to App Intents protocols, directly or through protocols that refine them.
 ///
 /// Types conforming to these protocols are discovered and invoked by the system at runtime,
 /// so they should not be reported as unused.
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ final class AppIntentsRetainer: SourceGraphMutator {
             .declarations(ofKinds: [.class, .struct, .enum])
             .lazy
             .filter {
-                $0.related.contains {
+                self.graph.inheritedTypeReferences(of: $0).contains {
                     self.graph.isExternal($0) &&
                         $0.declarationKind == .protocol &&
                         $0.usr.hasPrefix(Self.appIntentsModuleUsrPrefix)
